## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical Compose performance debugging, not just theory.

## Key Concepts

- Compose recomposition profiling
- Stable keys in LazyColumn
- Extracting item composables
- Immutable data models with stable ids
- Derived state and remember patterns
- SnapshotFlow and diffing for list updates

## Code Example

```kotlin
data class Article(val id: String, val title: String, val body: String)

@Composable
fun ArticleRow(article: Article) {
  Text(text = article.title)
}

@Composable
fun NewsFeed(articles: List<Article>) {
  LazyColumn { 
    items(articles, key = { it.id }) { article ->
      ArticleRow(article)
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure the impact of introducing a DiffUtil-like mechanism for the list?
- What edge cases could cause misleading recomposition counts and how would you guard against them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests basic Android data persistence and UI wiring using familiar components.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, database
- LiveData and ViewModel
- Repository pattern
- Prepopulation via RoomDatabase.Callback
- Rotation handling with LiveData

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Task(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val text: String,
  val done: Boolean = false
)
@Dao
interface TaskDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Task") fun getAll(): LiveData<List<Task>>
  @Insert fun insert(task: Task): Long
  @Delete fun delete(task: Task)
}
@Database(entities = [Task::class], version = 1)
abstract class AppDb : RoomDatabase() {
  abstract fun taskDao(): TaskDao
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test prepopulation and DAO methods?
- How would you migration plan for Task schema changes?

